==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} ''[[nudius]] [[tertius]]'', which is formed from the phrase ''[[nunc]] [[dies]] [[tertius]] [[est]]'', (now is the third day).

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{context|rare|obsolete|lang=en}} Of the [[day before yesterday]].
#: 1647 WARD Simp. Cobler 26 ''When I heare a..Gentledame inquire..what [is] the nudiustertian fashion of the Court; I mean the very newest.''

